#### procgen_kuratowski_20260925_kohl_tait.py
====================================================================================================
K1  generators, vertex types, Schreier graph = undirected C-graph on Z \ 0(6)
====================================================================================================
  a, b, c are involutions on |n| <= 60000
  class pairs 1(2)|4(6), 1(3)|2(6), 2(3)|4(6) are disjoint
  residue mod 6 -> moving generators (degree), semi-edges:
    0: moved by -   degree 0   semi-edges abc
    1: moved by ab  degree 2   semi-edges c
    2: moved by bc  degree 2   semi-edges a
    3: moved by a   degree 1   semi-edges bc
    4: moved by abc degree 3   semi-edges -
    5: moved by ac  degree 2   semi-edges b
  Schreier multigraph == undirected C-multigraph on (Z \ 0(6)) cap [-60000,60000]: 60000 edges
  the only multi-edge: [(-2, -1)] (the C 2-cycle -1 -> -2 -> -1)
  C maps N \ 0(6) into itself; C^{-1}(0(3)) = 0(6): multiples of 3 are transient (0(6) rays hang off the leaves 3(6))

====================================================================================================
K2  cycles and their colours
====================================================================================================
  every n in [1,200000] reaches the cycle (1 4 2); on N \ 0(6) the only cycle met is the triangle
  triangle colours: [(1, 4, 'a'), (4, 2, 'c'), (2, 1, 'b')]
  C-cycles met from [-200000,-1]: 3
    length  2: (-1, -2)
               colour word (C-direction): ac   counts {'a': 1, 'c': 1}
    length  5: (-5, -14, -7, -20, -10)
               colour word (C-direction): acacb   counts {'a': 2, 'c': 2, 'b': 1}
    length 18: (-17, -50, -25, -74, -37, -110, -55, -164, -82, -41, -122, -61, -182, -91, -272, -136, -68, -34)
               colour word (C-direction): acacacacbacacacbcb   counts {'a': 7, 'c': 8, 'b': 3}
  (0 is the C-fixed point; 0 in 0(6) is removed by Kohl)

====================================================================================================
K3  Kempe chains (orbits of the dihedral groups <b,c>, <a,b>, <a,c>)
====================================================================================================
  checked every vertex of (Z \ 0(6)) cap [-60000,60000] (100000 vertices):
   <b,c>: the doubling ray {o 2^j} of the odd part o (b/c alternate: 2 = -1 mod 3), singleton if 3 | o
   <a,b>: P_n = {2n (if n = 1 mod 6), n, 3n+1, 6n+2}, a path with 3 or 2 edges and exactly one a-edge
   <a,c>: the odd run y, 3y+1, T(y), ..., T^k(y) with k = v2(y+1), y = 1,3 mod 6; 2k edges
  closed Kempe chains found: [('ac', (-2, -1)), ('ac', (-2, -1))]
  two Kempe steps c,a from x = 5 mod 6 give E(x) = (2x-1)/3; b/c steps along a ray are D(x) = 2x:
  <a,c>-chains are maximal E-orbit segments, <b,c>-chains are D-orbits; D fixes 0 (in 0(6), deleted),
  E fixes -1 (the digon). v2(y+1) = -log2|y+1|_2: the <a,c> chain through y has 2k edges with 2^-k = |y+1|_2.
  Mersenne start y = 2^k - 1 opens the <a,c> chain of length 2k ending at 3^k - 1 (k = 1..11 checked)
  run-parameter k = v2(y+1) over starts y <= X: {1: 10000, 2: 5000, 3: 2500, 4: 1250, 5: 625, 6: 313, 7: 156, 8: 78}

====================================================================================================
K4  Kempe quotients
====================================================================================================
  K/<b,c>: vertices = odd numbers (rays), edges = a-edges {n, S(n)}, S = Syracuse map: the undirected Syracuse graph
  K/<a,b>: vertices = odd n (chains P_n), edges = c-edges; every edge is {n,4n+1}, {n,T(n)} (n=3 mod 4)
           or {n,T^2(n)} (n=1 mod 8); degree 3 if 3 does not divide n, 2 if n = 3 mod 6 (checked |n| <= X/8)
           P_1 carries a loop (the c-edge {2,4} of the triangle) and the edge {1,5}
  K/<a,c>: vertices = odd runs (start y = 1,3 mod 6), edges = b-edges; degree 1 + [y = 1 mod 6] + v2(y+1)
  connectivity of K <=> connectivity of each quotient (chains are connected); the loop/triangle survives in each

====================================================================================================
K5  the Z2 x Z2 boundary of the Tait colouring (a=(1,0), b=(0,1), c=(1,1))
====================================================================================================
  boundary delta(v) = sum of the colours at v = sum of the missing colours:
    v = 1 mod 6: delta = ['c']
    v = 2 mod 6: delta = ['a']
    v = 3 mod 6: delta = ['a']
    v = 4 mod 6: delta = ['0']
    v = 5 mod 6: delta = ['b']
  the colouring is a nowhere-zero Z2^2-flow exactly at the branch points 4(6) (two C-preimages);
  every other vertex is a source: 1,2,5 mod 6 (degree 2) and the leaves 3(6) (degree 1)

====================================================================================================
K6  switches: Kempe switches keep the graph; nu and single-colour conjugations change it
====================================================================================================
  Kempe switch a<->b on the chains P_n, n = 1 mod 4: new involutions a', b' (rcwa, modulus of a' = 24),
  a' != a at 50000 window points, Schreier graph identical (139999 edges): transitivity is unchanged.
  nu a nu = a^h0 = tau_{1(2),2(6)} (n <-> 3n-1), nu b nu = c, nu c nu = b, with h0 = tau_{2(6),4(6)}:
  nu G_C nu = <a^h0, c, b> = G_C^- (the 3n-1 group); the sheet swap = one-colour conjugation of a by the
  '+-2' class transposition h0, composed with the global Kempe relabelling b <-> c (which keeps the graph).
  3n-1 C-cycles met from [1,20000]: [(1, 2), (5, 14, 7, 20, 10), (17, 50, 25, 74, 37, 110, '...')]
  => G_C^- = <tau_{1(2),2(6)}, b, c> has >= 3 orbits on N \ 0(6) (PROVED: three distinct cycles)
  single-colour switch census: h = tau_{c1,c2}, c1,c2 disjoint classes inside 2(6) u 4(6), support meeting 4(6);
  F_h(n) = h(3n+1) (n odd), n/2 (n even) is the map whose functional graph is the Schreier graph of <a^h,b,c>.
  columns: up-slopes | Haar log-drift of the odd->odd map | cycles met from [1,3000] | escapes past 1e30
   tau_{2(6),4(6)}: odd n -> 3n-1 [n=1 mod 2]
        Haar drift -0.287  cycles 3 (min, length) [(1, 2), (5, 5), (17, 18)]  escapes    0  => SHEET-type (>=2 cycles, PROVED intransitive)
   tau_{2(6),4(12)}: odd n -> (3n+1)/2 [n=1 mod 4]; 3n+1 [n=3 mod 4]
        Haar drift -0.288  cycles 1 (min, length) [(1, 2)]  escapes    0  => Collatz-like (1 cycle; OPEN)
   tau_{2(6),10(12)}: odd n -> (3n-5)/2 [n=3 mod 4]; 3n+1 [n=1 mod 4]
        Haar drift -0.980  cycles 1 (min, length) [(1, 3)]  escapes    0  => PROVED transitive (odd-step descent beyond n0 = 1)
   tau_{4(6),2(12)}: odd n -> 6n-4 [n=1 mod 2]
        Haar drift +1.099  cycles 1 (min, length) [(1, 2)]  escapes 2988  => DRIFT-type, PROVED divergent beyond n1 = 1 (one-step ascent) => PROVED intransitive
   tau_{4(6),8(12)}: odd n -> 6n+2 [n=1 mod 2]
        Haar drift -0.287  cycles 1 (min, length) [(1, 4)]  escapes    0  => Collatz-like (1 cycle; OPEN)
   tau_{2(12),4(12)}: odd n -> 3n-1 [n=1 mod 4]; 3n+1 [n=3 mod 4]
        Haar drift +0.405  cycles 1 (min, length) [(1, 2)]  escapes 2988  => DRIFT-type, PROVED divergent beyond n1 = 1 (one-step ascent) => PROVED intransitive
   tau_{2(12),10(12)}: odd n -> 3n-7 [n=3 mod 4]; 3n+1 [n=1 mod 4]
        Haar drift -0.287  cycles 4 (min, length) [(1, 3), (7, 2), (19, 5), (23, 10)]  escapes    0  => SHEET-type (>=2 cycles, PROVED intransitive)
   tau_{4(12),8(12)}: odd n -> 3n+1 [n=3 mod 4]; 3n+5 [n=1 mod 4]
        Haar drift -0.287  cycles 4 (min, length) [(1, 4), (5, 3), (7, 8), (47, 13)]  escapes    0  => SHEET-type (>=2 cycles, PROVED intransitive)
   tau_{4(12),10(12)}: odd n -> 3n-5 [n=3 mod 4]; 3n+7 [n=1 mod 4]
        Haar drift -0.287  cycles 3 (min, length) [(1, 12), (17, 8), (41, 39)]  escapes    0  => SHEET-type (>=2 cycles, PROVED intransitive)
   tau_{8(12),10(12)}: odd n -> 3n-1 [n=3 mod 4]; 3n+1 [n=1 mod 4]
        Haar drift -0.980  cycles 1 (min, length) [(1, 3)]  escapes    0  => PROVED transitive (odd-step descent beyond n0 = 1)
  (control: Collatz itself fails the descent test -- n = 3 mod 4 has s/2^k = 3/2)
  the four mod-4 sign strategies of Althofer's 3n+-1 game are one-colour switches of G_C:
    (+,+) identity           : 3n+1                       -> Collatz (OPEN)
    (-,-) tau_{2(6),4(6)}    : 3n-1                       -> SHEET-type (>=2 cycles, PROVED intransitive)
    (-,+) tau_{2(12),4(12)}  : 3n-1 (n=1 mod 4), 3n+1 (n=3 mod 4): one halving each -> DRIFT-type, PROVED divergent beyond n1 = 1 (one-step ascent) => PROVED intransitive
    (+,-) tau_{8(12),10(12)} : 3n+1 (n=1 mod 4), 3n-1 (n=3 mod 4): 4 | 3n+-1        -> PROVED transitive (odd-step descent beyond n0 = 1)
  => Collatz is one corner of a square whose three other corners are PROVED (two intransitive, one transitive).
  moduli 6..24: 114 switches: {'SHEET-type (>=2 cycles: PROVED intransitive)': 48, 'Collatz-like (1 cycle, no escapes; OPEN)': 37, 'PROVED transitive (odd-step descent)': 3, 'DRIFT-type, PROVED divergent (one-step ascent)': 8, 'DRIFT-type (positive drift, escapes; heuristic)': 16, 'mixed (escapes with negative drift, or none)': 2}
  no class-transposition switch is a DEFECT control: a nonidentity rcwa change has positive-density support.

====================================================================================================
K7  Kohl's mod-3 shape <a_q, b, c> tracks C_q (qn+1) only when 3 | q; the mod-p generalisation
====================================================================================================
  q = 3: a_q = tau_{1(2),4(6)}; odd n with qn+1 = 0 mod 3: none
  q = 5: a_q = tau_{1(2),6(10)}; odd n with qn+1 = 0 mod 3: [1, 7, 13, 19]
  q = 9: a_q = tau_{1(2),10(18)}; odd n with qn+1 = 0 mod 3: none
  q = 5: C_5 path 7 -> 36 -> 18 -> 9 -> 46; in <a_5,b,c>: 36 has neighbours [7] , 18 has none (isolated)
  so the q = 5 Kohl-shape (mod-3) group cuts C_5-orbits (18 is a fixed point of all three generators):
  Kohl's mod-3 shape needs 3 | q (multiples of 3 transient) as well as 2 = -1 mod 3 (doubling flips the sign).
  mod-p generalisation: {m,2m} (p not dividing m) can be 2-coloured properly by m mod p iff -1 is a power of 2
  mod p (the doubling cycles on (Z/p)^x have even length): p=3:yes, p=5:yes, p=7:no, p=11:yes, p=13:yes, p=17:yes, p=19:yes, p=23:no, p=29:yes, p=31:no, p=37:yes, p=41:yes, p=43:yes, p=47:no
  q = 5 with p = 5: <tau_{1(2),6(10)}, b_5, c_5> (b_5, c_5 = doubling split by the parity of log_2 m mod 5)
  has Schreier graph = the C_5-graph on Z \ 0(10) (window |n| <= 20000), multiples of 5 transient;
  it is intransitive on N \ 0(10) (cycles through 1, 13, 17): the Tait framework is DRIFT-blind as well.

