====================================================================================================
U1  the sign fold pi(x) = |x| and the dodecahedron -> Petersen control
====================================================================================================
  pi is a graph homomorphism Gamma_+ -> U on |x| <= 30000; (edge type, sheet, multiplicity) -> #U-edges:
     ('halving', 'neg', 1) 14999
     ('halving', 'pos', 1) 14999
     ('halving=up- (the digon {1,2})', 'neg', 2) 1
     ('halving=up- (the digon {1,2})', 'pos', 1) 1
     ('up+', 'pos', 1) 5000
     ('up-', 'neg', 1) 4999
  local deficit deg_U(|x|) - deg_Gamma+(x) equals 1 exactly at x = 1,2,3,5 mod 6 and 0 at x = 0,4 mod 6,
  for all 0 < |x| <= 7500, the only exceptions being [1, 2] (the simple-graph digon {1,2})
  => pi is locally injective but not locally surjective: an immersion (fold), not a covering; the
     deficit set 1,2,3,5 mod 6 is exactly the support of Kohl's Tait boundary delta (part K5):
     the fold attaches the other sheet's up-edge at every Tait defect.
  W = Gamma_+ u Gamma_- -> U is locally bijective (a covering) with deck involution nu, but no W-edge joins
     x > 0 to y < 0: W = U + nu(U), the TRIVIAL double cover (every Collatz-type move preserves sign).
  control: dodecahedron -> dodecahedron/antipode = Petersen is a CONNECTED double covering (planar cover of a
     nonplanar graph). The Collatz sign cover is disconnected, so the analogy fails at the key point.

