#### procgen_kuratowski_20260925_triples.py
====================================================================================================
T1  KT-a in graphs
====================================================================================================
  contracting the 5 spokes (a perfect matching) of Petersen gives K5
  Petersen contains a K33 subdivision (branch vertices [2, 3, 6, 7, 8, 9] ) -- never a K5 subdivision (cubic)
  K5 and K33 are minor-incomparable (5 < 6 vertices; 9 < 10 edges)
  Delta-Y on a triangle of K5 gives K33 + one edge (the extra edge (3, 4) ): the twins are one
  star-triangle (Kennelly 1899, electrical) move apart, up to an edge
  the Delta-Y / Y-Delta class of K6 has 7 graphs (vertices: [6, 7, 7, 8, 8, 9, 10] ) and contains Petersen: the Petersen family
  (CITED, Wikipedia pages read 2026-09-25: these 7 are the forbidden minors for linkless embedding [RST],
   and for Colin de Verdiere mu <= 4 [Lovasz-Schrijver 1998]; mu <= 3 <=> planar <=> no K5, K33 minor.)

====================================================================================================
T2  KT-b in matroids (Tutte 1958/1965: regular <=> no U24, F7, F7*; graphic adds M*(K5), M*(K33))
====================================================================================================
  F7 (7 nonzero vectors of GF(2)^3): rank 3; its dual F7* has rank 7 - 3 = 4: a dual PAIR
  U_{2,4}: dual is U_{4-2,4} = U_{2,4}: SELF-DUAL
  M(K5): rank 4, corank 6; M*(K5) is regular, not graphic
  M(K33): rank 5, corank 4; M*(K33) is regular, not graphic
  => Tutte's regular-matroid triple {F7, F7*, U24} is exactly KT-b: a dual pair plus a self-dual third

====================================================================================================
T3  sheets b in {-1, 0, +1}
====================================================================================================
  nu T_b nu = T_{-b} on Z for b = 1, 3, 5 (|x| <= 5000): nu swaps the sheets +-1
  the central sheet b = 0 (x -> x/2 or 3x/2) commutes with nu: SELF-DUAL; so {-1,0,+1} is KT-b exactly.
  It is not KT-a: b = 0 is the common scaling limit (x -> lambda x, lambda -> inf) of BOTH sheets, i.e. BELOW
  them (a degeneration), not a container above them.

====================================================================================================
T4  means GM, AM, QM
====================================================================================================
  QM^2 + GM^2 = 2 AM^2; the involution s -> 2 AM^2 - s swaps GM^2 <-> QM^2 and fixes AM^2: KT-b exactly
  (the parallelogram law (a+b)^2 + (a-b)^2 = 2a^2 + 2b^2: the sign of the cross term +-2ab is the swap;
   THM-4471 puts the sign law in exactly this cross term)

