M1  the rcwa minor relation on two-branch maps
====================================================================================================
  T_{q,r}(d x) = d T_{q,r/d}(x) for every odd d | r (q = 1,3,5,7; r = 3,5,9,15,21,25; |x| <= 3000):
  (q, r/d) is the restriction of (q, r) to the invariant set dZ, conjugated by x -> x/d
  the multiplier q is a minor invariant (restriction and affine conjugation keep the affine slopes q/2, 1/2),
  so the q-slices are pairwise incomparable: {(q, 1) : q odd} is an infinite ANTICHAIN (no wqo, no
  Robertson-Seymour finiteness for this order).

