====================================================================================================
M3  Conn (single grand orbit on N): excluded minors
====================================================================================================
  codes: X2 = two cycles found (NOT Conn), Xp = invariant pN with invariant complement (NOT Conn),
         ok = one cycle and no escape (consistent with Conn), ?e = escapes (status open)
  for primes p not dividing 2q, x in pN <=> T_{q,p}(x) in pN (checked q = 1,3,5,7, p <= 25, x <= 20000):
  both pN and N \ pN are unions of grand orbits, so (q, p) is never Conn (PROVED for all such q, p).
  q = 1: r=1..25 -> 1:ok 3:X2 5:X2 7:X2 9:X2 11:X2 13:X2 15:X2 17:X2 19:X2 21:X2 23:X2 25:X2
         minimal non-Conn r (excluded minors of the slice, r <= 25): [3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19, 23]
  q = 3: r=1..25 -> 1:ok 3:ok 5:X2 7:X2 9:ok 11:X2 13:X2 15:X2 17:X2 19:X2 21:X2 23:X2 25:X2
         minimal non-Conn r (excluded minors of the slice, r <= 25): [5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19, 23]
  q = 5: r=1..25 -> 1:X2 3:X2 5:X2 7:X2 9:X2 11:X2 13:X2 15:X2 17:X2 19:X2 21:X2 23:X2 25:X2
         minimal non-Conn r (excluded minors of the slice, r <= 25): [1]
  q = 7: r=1..25 -> 1:?e 3:Xp 5:X2 7:?e 9:X2 11:X2 13:Xp 15:X2 17:Xp 19:X2 21:Xp 23:X2 25:X2
         minimal non-Conn r (excluded minors of the slice, r <= 25): [3, 5, 11, 13, 17, 19, 23]
  (q = 1: r = 1 is PROVED Conn; q = 3: r = 1 is Collatz; q = 7: r = 1 is open, so its list is conditional)
  q = 3: if Collatz holds, (3,1) is Conn and the excluded minors of the slice are {(3,p): p prime >= 5},
  an infinite antichain; if Collatz fails, (3,1) itself is the unique excluded minor of the slice.
  So 'the q = 3 slice has a finite Kuratowski set' <=> 'Collatz is false' -- a restatement, not a reduction.
  The SHEET control (3,-1) on N and the DRIFT control (5,1) are ATOMS (r = 1) and non-Conn: genuine excluded
  minors (PROVED by their extra cycles); they are incomparable (different sheet / different multiplier).

