M4  the three controls and their independence
====================================================================================================
  epsilon (single flip of pair 4 = {7,8}): cycles met from starts < 3000: [(1, 2), (3, 5, 6, 8, 12)]
  epsilon (density-zero flips, THM-4470(4)): c_0 = 3, c_(t+1) = c_t + ceil(c_t/2), flip the pair of every even
  c_t: the orbit of 3 is c_0 < c_1 < ... (300 steps verified, c_300 ~ 10^53); flipped pairs
  below 10^30: 81 (density zero)
  epsilon C is not rcwa: an rcwa map agreeing with T on a density-one set agrees with T on every residue
  class where both are affine, i.e. everywhere; epsilon C differs from T on the flipped pairs.

  system                     drift sign  b*side  rcwa   status
  C = (3,+1) on N                     -      +1  True   Collatz (OPEN)
  sigma C = (3,-1) on N               -      -1  True   NOT Conn: 3 cycles
  delta C = (5,+1) on N               +      +1  True   NOT Conn: 3 cycles
  epsilon C = flips of T              -      +1 False   NOT Conn: new cycle / divergent orbit

  which invariant separates C from which control (True = separates):
    drift sign: sigma False  delta True   epsilon False
    b*side    : sigma True   delta False  epsilon False
    rcwa      : sigma False  delta False  epsilon True 
  => each invariant separates exactly one control: the controls are pairwise independent (separating one
     never forces separating another), and a sound method proving Collatz must see all three kinds of data:
     the archimedean order (sheet), size with the multiplier (drift), and pointwise/non-density data (defect).

